XST: The Xtrata Participation Token

XST is the native token of the Xtrata protocol.

It is not sold, not pre-mined, and not controlled by anyone.

It exists for one reason only:

To permanently reward early participation in Xtrata.

⸻

How many XST tokens exist?

Exactly 1 billion.

No more can ever be created.

⸻

When do tokens start being created?

XST does not start immediately.

Token emissions begin only after the 100th inscription is created.

That moment starts a fixed, public countdown.

⸻

How long do emissions last?

Exactly 4 years.

After that:
	•	no new tokens are created
	•	forever

This is guaranteed by the contract.

⸻

How are tokens distributed?

Every 10 minutes (roughly one block), a small number of XST tokens are released.

Those tokens are split into two pools:
	•	70% goes to inscription owners
	•	30% goes to active participants

⸻

Why do early inscriptions earn more?

Each inscription earns tokens based on its inscription number.

Earlier inscription numbers have slightly higher weight.

This means:
	•	Inscription #0 earns the most
	•	#1–10 earn slightly less
	•	#11–100 slightly less again
	•	And so on, smoothly and predictably

This weighting never changes.

If you buy an early inscription later, you inherit its earning power.

⸻

What about people who join later?

Later participants still earn XST.

The participant pool ensures:
	•	holding even one inscription earns tokens
	•	rewards grow slowly and fairly
	•	no one wallet can dominate

⸻

Can anyone change the rules?

No.

Once deployed:
	•	the supply is fixed
	•	the schedule is fixed
	•	the weights are fixed
	•	even the creator cannot change them

⸻

What happens after 4 years?

Emissions stop.

XST becomes a fixed historical token that represents:
	•	who was early
	•	who participated
	•	and how Xtrata grew

At that point, XST is no longer about rewards —
it’s about history.

⸻

Final note

XST is not a promise of profit.

It is a record of participation.

If Xtrata matters, XST will matter —
because it proves you were there.

